<p>Random marketing is the single biggest problem facing Kenyan SMEs today. It looks like this: boosting a Facebook post because a competitor did it. Running Google Ads for a month, stopping because "it did not work." Hiring a social media manager who posts quotes on Instagram every day with zero measurable outcome. Trying every tactic without a clear strategy connecting them. This framework ends that.</p>

<h2>What is Random Marketing?</h2>

<p>Random marketing is characterised by:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Activity without strategy — doing things because others are doing them</li>
  <li>No clear audience definition — trying to reach "everyone"</li>
  <li>Channel-first thinking — "we need to be on TikTok" before asking why</li>
  <li>No measurement — unable to tell what is working and what is not</li>
  <li>Inconsistency — starting campaigns and stopping them before results compound</li>
  <li>Disconnected efforts — SEO, social media and ads operating in silos</li>
</ul>

<p>The result: money is spent, activity happens, but revenue does not grow proportionally. The marketing feels like a cost, not an investment.</p>

